.TH INVF-LS 1 "2026-09" "InvariantFS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
invf\-ls, invf\-cat, invf\-cp, invf\-stat \- read\-side CLI utilities for InvariantFS volumes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invf\-ls
.I image
.br
.B invf\-cat
.I image
.I name
.RI [ output\-file ]
.br
.B invf\-cp
.I image
.I host\-file
.RI [ name\-in\-volume ]
.br
.B invf\-stat
.I image
.RB [ \-\-files ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
These tools read data from an InvariantFS volume without requiring a FUSE
mount. They operate directly on the volume image or block device.
.SS invf\-ls
Lists every live file on the volume with its size, inode number, and name.
Container members (virtual windows) are listed when present.
.SS invf\-cat
Extracts a named file from the volume to
.IR output\-file ,
or to stdout if omitted. For container members containing
.BR ! ,
tries inode lookup first, then falls back to container\-member extraction.
.SS invf\-cp
Copies a host file into the volume. If
.I name\-in\-volume
is omitted, the host filename is used. If the name already exists, the
old content is overwritten.
.SS invf\-stat
Displays a console\-level space inspector with ANSI\-colored block
category bars (RAW, semantic, dedup, free) and population counts.
.IP "\fB\-\-files\fR" 4
Additionally list each file with its policy tag and size.
.SH EXIT STATUS
All four tools exit 0 on success, 1 on I/O or volume errors, 2 on
usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf\-fuse (8),
.BR invf\-sweep (8),
.BR invarifs (7)
